    "qt": "6.12.0",
    "version": "14.5.0",
    "assessment": "Affected code is not built or shipped. CVE-2026-113679 is an out-of-bounds host write through the font_glyph_to_string WAMR import of HarfBuzz's experimental WebAssembly shaper (hb-wasm-api-font.hh, registered by hb-wasm-api-list.hh and compiled only into hb-wasm-api.cc/hb-wasm-shape.cc under HAVE_WASM). Qt 6.12.0's BundledHarfbuzz target compiles 70 HarfBuzz sources, none of them hb-wasm-*, and defines no HAVE_WASM, so hb-shaper-list.hh registers only the ot and fallback shapers. The official Qt 6.12.0 binaries were configured -qt-harfbuzz; the AppImage's libQt6Gui.so.6 is that official file byte for byte, links no libharfbuzz or WAMR library and contains none of the shaper's import names.",
    "decision": "Scoped disposition, not an update: no Qt release carries HarfBuzz 15.0.0 (v6.12.0 ships 14.5.0; the 6.12 and dev branches 14.6.0, also affected), and rebuilding qtbase against a newer HarfBuzz would replace the official Qt binaries, their SBOM-based notices and ABI with the official Qt Wayland/SVG/image format modules for code that is not compiled. Revisit when a Qt release ships HarfBuzz >= 15.0.0.",
    "upstreamFix": {
      "repository": "https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz",
