    "qt": "6.12.0",
    "version": "3.53.4",
    "assessment": "CVE-2026-119379 is in the session extension, which is not built: Qt 6.12.0's driver does not define SQLITE_ENABLE_SESSION. CVE-2026-119373 and CVE-2026-119374 are in FTS5, which is built (SQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5) but not reached: put.gd has no FTS tables, virtual tables, ATTACH or load_extension, and its one QSQLITE connection site (HistoryStore) opens only history.sqlite in put.gd's own owner-only data folder. Triggering them takes a crafted database in that place, which means an attacker already running as the user.",
    "decision": "Scoped disposition accepted by Patrick for the first stable, not an update: no Qt release carries SQLite 3.54 (v6.12.0 ships 3.53.4; the 6.12 branch has 3.54.1), and replacing the official driver would change its source, notices and SBOM just before release. Revisit when a Qt release ships SQLite >= 3.54.0. Unlike the HarfBuzz disposition, the FTS5 code does ship.",
